Then we see that each row, each column and each diagonal consists of a chess piece. This proves $r = 2n$ when $n$ is even.

**Case 2.** $n = 2k + 1$ is odd
Consider the following $2n + 2$ diagonals:
$$
\begin{aligned}
\{(i,j) : i + j = m\} & \quad \text{for } m = 2, 3, \dots, k + 2, \\
\{(i,j) : j - i = m\} & \quad \text{for } m = k, k + 1, \dots, 2k, \\
