UPDATE public.questoes SET solucao = 'First we will prove a lemma which is a generalized form of the given problem. Let $|\Omega|$ be the universal set.

**Lemma:** If $a_1 \leq |A| \leq a_2$; $b_1 \leq |B| \leq b_2$ then the double inequality
$$
\max\{0, a_1 + a_2 - |\Omega|\} \leq |A \cap B| \leq \min\{a_2, b_2\}
$$
holds.

**Proof of lemma:**

a) Obviously $|A \cap B| \leq \min\{|A|, |B|\}$. Equality holds when either $A \subset B$ or $B \subset A$.

b) Let us prove that $\max\{|A| + |B| - |\Omega|, 0\} \leq |A \cap B|$. Consider the case $|A| + |B| - |\Omega| < 0$. If $A \cap B = \emptyset$ then $|A \cap B| = 0$.

Consider the case $|A| + |B| - |\Omega| \geq 0$. Then by inclusion-exclusion principle
$$
|A \cap B| = |A| + |B| - |A \cup B| \geq |A| + |B| - |\Omega|
$$
and we have done.

Now let us apply the lemma to the given problem. Let $|A|, |B|, |C|$ be percent of students who solved I, II, III problems respectively. Then our task is to find minimal and maximal value of $|A \cap B \cap C|$.

First, consider $|A| = 98\%$, $|B| = 90\%$.
By the aforementioned lemma:
$$
\max\{0, 98\% + 90\% - 100\%\} \leq |A \cap B| \leq \min\{98\%, 90\%\}
$$
So $88\% \leq |A \cap B| \leq 90\%$.
Now, $|A \cap B|$ and $|C| = 85\%$.
Apply the lemma again:
$$
\max\{0, 88\% + 85\% - 100\%\} \leq |A \cap B \cap C| \leq \min\{90\%, 85\%\}
$$
So $73\% \leq |A \cap B \cap C| \leq 85\%$.

Thus, the least percentage of students that solved all three problems is $73\%$, and the most is $85\%$.' WHERE id = 6828;
