Now, we can repeat the arguments from the last paragraph: Because of (iv) we have $c_{5} \neq 9$. By $(*)$ and (ii) we have $b_{3} \neq 9$ (otherwise $a_{3}<c_{a_{3}}=b_{3}+1=10$ and there is no number left for $a_{3}$ ). So we have $a_{3}=9$. By (iii), $a_{4} \neq 10$. By (ii), $c_{9}=c_{a_{3}}=b_{3}+1$, therefore $b_{3} \neq 10$ (otherwise there are no numbers left for $c_{5}, \ldots, c_{8}$ ). So we have $c_{5}=10$. Similarly
$$
\begin{aligned}
