| ...| ...| ...| ...| ...| ...|

Note that the fifth person in each test can become a team member, only if all the other four persons above already have been chosen as a team member. Therefore, to prove that the example works, it suffices to show that the fifth person in each test can become a team member. For each of the students $9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14$, consider these permutations of tests

$$
\begin{array}{l}
