$\angle CPD = \angle CPQ'' + \angle Q''PD = \angle Q''DA + \angle Q''AD = \angle BQ''A.$
So $\angle BPD = \angle CQ''A$. Also $BD$ bisects $\angle CQ''A$. Let us show that $Q''=Q$. Assume these points are distinct. Because of the fact that
